in this crazy mixed-up world amusement  parks can be our escape from the trials  of our normal lives the smell of popcorn  the deafening roar of rollercoasters it  all makes me happier than a kid in the  candy store but if there's one thing I  love more than visiting amusement parks  it's building them roller coaster tycoon  star that love affair for me back in  1999 and the newest game by UK developer  frontier looks a continuing now the guys  at frontier are no strangers to theme  park games they're responsible for many  of the roller coaster tycoon games as  well as thrill ville scream ride and  several other mobile titles the last  couple of years found them working on  the sci-fi epic elite dangerous but with  their new game planet coaster they've  returned to the theme park building sim  world and they're looking to reclaim the  throne as coaster building king  newcomers to the genre will find it easy  to start building right away as the  game's friendly UI makes it easy to  construct their own park from scratch  there are quite a few pre-made shops and  coaster tracks that just plop down in  front of a walkway as well as tons of  scenery options to fill out all the  empty space in between rides but like  any good simulation game it's when you  take a closer look at the details does  planet coaster truly shine the game  offers levels upon levels upon levels of  micromanaging from staff training to  refurbishing rides to even the salary of  your burger vendor your park is truly  your own and planet coaster does an  amazing job by giving you all the  control you could ever want  in addition planet coaster offers an  unprecedented of customization right  down to the rotation of your garden  lights the game gives you complete  control over every little detail in the  park and thanks to the Steam Workshop  the games developers have opened the  door for seemingly unlimited  possibilities with user-generated  content by embracing the modding  community people are now able to create  and share their own personal concoctions  with players all over the world in  developer interviews frontières stated  that they're focusing a lot of their  attention on the individual guests  unlike a lot of other simulation games  they're not  taking any shortcuts in making the parks  guests just as important as the rest of  the game  everything from the individual character  designed to the crowd fluidity to the  walk emotions have all been crafted with  the utmost care injecting some  much-needed personality into the genre  and because of the effort put into  making them feel like actual people  rather than just mindless cash drones  the game feels so much more alive  now I love the original rollercoaster  tycoon  it's one of my favorite games of all  time but that game was all about the  park it was about building the coolest  coasters and rides and making the most  money in the sense it was all about the  business sure the game supplied hundreds  upon hundreds of people to populate your  park but they were mostly there for  giving you money and vomiting all over  the place in fact now that I think about  it the people in these tycoon games feel  more like a responsibility than anything  else you entertain them you clean up  after them you keep them safe most of  the time and while it's true that the  main goal is to get them to enjoy the  park and all the rides in it the only  way that they can validate their  enjoyment is with their wallet of course  that doesn't take anything away from the  game tycoon games have been and always  will be about the business they're about  money first and people's second which is  why planet coaster feels so special to  me it's a simulation game focused around  the experience of being in a theme park  rather than owning one you might not be  the actual guests but more than ever you  can feel what they feel as you put your  finishing touches on a ride that you  spend hours constructing the payoff is  not only monetary but also emotional you  can see the guests reactions while  riding a coaster whether they're  enjoying it or screaming terror they'll  run towards newly opened rides hoping to  be first in line and hey remember that  burger vendor whose salary we increased  we actually see her enthusiasm for  working there  in the game not just as a colored bar  that says happy yes you still have to  manage your finances wrangle your park  staff and occasionally deal with the  tidal wave puke but the game's  presentation might be the defining  feature planet coaster seeing the guests  excitement and reaction to rides things  that I have built myself and spent hours  upon hours creating is way more  rewarding than any profit chart could be  and when the game can connect to me on a  personal level especially one coming  from a genre that glorifies staring at  numbers and charts it's done something  right so while other themed Park games  have encountered some problems as of  late it's comforting to know that  another game will be there to step up  and leave the amusement parks image  planet coaster is a game that rose out  of necessity and it looks to fill that  gaping hole in my heart that so many  previous theme park games left behind  the game is beautiful it's deep and it's  every bit as fun as the first roller  coaster tycoon was for me over 15 years  ago for more on plan coaster and  everything else video games stay tuned  the GameSpot and thanks for watching  you
 

